# Files whose merge conflicts are two branches each adding lines: keep both sides' lines (git's built-in `union` merge)
# instead of stopping at a conflict. It applies to local merges (`git merge`); GitHub's own "Update branch" may not
# honour it. Not for a file where order matters beyond the lines themselves, and the tests still say when both sides'
# lines together are wrong (a decision number used twice). A conflict resolved by hand that leaves a marker fails
# tools/conflict-markers.test.ts.
# Lifted from yggi/cells .gitattributes @ 6ea7ab9.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
docs/MEMORY.md merge=union
